    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p45-q6-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1 x(x+1)^3\\,dx$, using $x=u-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{49}{20}$",
          "worked": "$x=u-1$, so $dx=du$. When $x=0$, $u=1$; when $x=1$, $u=2$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\int_0^1x(x+1)^3\\,dx&=\\int_1^2(u-1)u^3\\,du\\\\&=\\int_1^2(u^4-u^3)\\,du\\\\&=\\left[\\frac{u^5}{5}-\\frac{u^4}{4}\\right]_1^2\\\\&=\\left(\\frac{32}{5}-4\\right)-\\left(\\frac15-\\frac14\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{49}{20}.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p45-q6-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\int_0^{1/2}\\frac{1+x}{1-x}\\,dx$, using $x=1-u$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2\\ln2-\\frac12$",
          "worked": "$x=1-u$, so $dx=-du$. When $x=0$, $u=1$; when $x=\\frac12$, $u=\\frac12$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\int_0^{1/2}\\frac{1+x}{1-x}\\,dx&=-\\int_1^{1/2}\\frac{2-u}{u}\\,du\\\\&=\\int_{1/2}^1\\left(\\frac2u-1\\right)\\,du\\\\&=[2\\ln u-u]_{1/2}^1\\\\&=-1-\\left(-2\\ln2-\\frac12\\right)\\\\&=2\\ln2-\\frac12.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p45-q6-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\frac{3x}{\\sqrt{3x+1}}\\,dx$, using $x=\\frac13(u-1)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac89$",
          "worked": "$x=\\frac13(u-1)$, so $dx=\\frac13\\,du$. When $x=0$, $u=1$; when $x=1$, $u=4$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\int_0^1\\frac{3x}{\\sqrt{3x+1}}\\,dx&=\\frac13\\int_1^4\\frac{u-1}{\\sqrt u}\\,du\\\\&=\\frac13\\int_1^4(u^{1/2}-u^{-1/2})\\,du\\\\&=\\frac13\\left[\\frac23u^{3/2}-2u^{1/2}\\right]_1^4\\\\&=\\frac13\\left[\\left(\\frac{16}{3}-4\\right)-\\left(\\frac23-2\\right)\\right]\\\\&=\\frac89.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p45-q6-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\frac{2-x}{(2+x)^3}\\,dx$, using $x=u-2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac19$",
          "worked": "$x=u-2$, so $dx=du$. When $x=0$, $u=2$; when $x=1$, $u=3$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\int_0^1\\frac{2-x}{(2+x)^3}\\,dx&=\\int_2^3\\frac{4-u}{u^3}\\,du\\\\&=\\int_2^3(4u^{-3}-u^{-2})\\,du\\\\&=\\left[-\\frac2{u^2}+\\frac1u\\right]_2^3\\\\&=\\left(-\\frac29+\\frac13\\right)-\\left(-\\frac12+\\frac12\\right)\\\\&=\\frac19.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p45-q6-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\int_0^4x\\sqrt{4-x}\\,dx$, using $x=4-u^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{128}{15}$",
          "worked": "Take $u=\\sqrt{4-x}\\geq0$. Then $dx=-2u\\,du$. When $x=0$, $u=2$; when $x=4$, $u=0$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\int_0^4x\\sqrt{4-x}\\,dx&=\\int_2^0(4-u^2)u(-2u)\\,du\\\\&=2\\int_0^2(4u^2-u^4)\\,du\\\\&=2\\left[\\frac{4u^3}{3}-\\frac{u^5}{5}\\right]_0^2\\\\&=2\\left(\\frac{32}{3}-\\frac{32}{5}\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{128}{15}.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p45-q6-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\int_1^5\\frac{x}{(2x-1)^{3/2}}\\,dx$, using $x=\\frac12(u^2+1)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac43$",
          "worked": "Take $u=\\sqrt{2x-1}>0$. Then $dx=u\\,du$. When $x=1$, $u=1$; when $x=5$, $u=3$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\int_1^5\\frac{x}{(2x-1)^{3/2}}\\,dx&=\\frac12\\int_1^3\\frac{u^2+1}{u^3}u\\,du\\\\&=\\frac12\\int_1^3(1+u^{-2})\\,du\\\\&=\\frac12\\left[u-\\frac1u\\right]_1^3\\\\&=\\frac12\\left[\\left(3-\\frac13\\right)-(1-1)\\right]\\\\&=\\frac43.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      }
    ]
